---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND_NAME } from '~/lib/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Editorial Policy | ${BRAND_NAME}`}
  description="How our content gets made: AI-assisted drafting, human review, mandatory sourcing, and a strict wall between money and coverage."
>
  <div class="wrap prose page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Trust</p>
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>

    <h2>How content is made</h2>
    <p>
      Our drafts are produced with AI assistance and researched against
      official sources — then reviewed, corrected, and approved by a human
      editor before anything is published. Nothing goes live without human
      sign-off. Every dog-policy fact must carry a recorded source; drafts
      that can't source a claim don't ship it.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      When we learn a published fact is wrong or out of date, we fix the page
      and update its verification date. Listings that can't be re-verified are
      removed rather than left to rot.
    </p>

    <h2>Money never buys coverage</h2>
    <p>
      Venues cannot pay to be listed, ranked, or described favorably. Ads are
      served by third-party networks and clearly separated from editorial
      content. Affiliate links (marked and disclosed) never influence whether
      a venue appears or what we say about its dog policy. If a venue with an
      affiliate program has a bad dog policy, we say so.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No pay-for-placement, ever.</li>
      <li>No copying policies from other directories.</li>
      <li>No AI-generated facts without a recorded source.</li>
      <li>No stock-photo pretending: photos are owner-supplied and licensed.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 2rem;
  }
</style>
